hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1372","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman al-Bakrawi told us, Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The sun was eclipsed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said The people: It was only broken by the death of Abraham, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and addressed the people, saying: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs. God, so when you see that, thank God, glorify God, glorify God, and pray until the eclipse of whichever of them is eclipsed.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended and prayed two rak’ahs."
